From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] client: Retain redirect targets for loop detection

The response line passed to handle_redirect is freed by
get_server_responses after the handler returns.  The redirect list
must own a copy of the root; otherwise its hash entry points to freed
memory and repeated redirects can loop forever.

Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
diff --git a/src/client.c b/src/client.c
--- a/src/client.c
+++ b/src/client.c
@@ -615 +615 @@ handle_redirect (char *args, size_t len)
-	push_string (redirects, args);
+	push_string (redirects, xstrdup (args));
